                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I have been a wargamer since the late 60's--yeah, old guy here...  I have learned over the years that simplicity and ease of play typically triumph over details, details, and more details.  Now, don't get me wrong--deep dive simulations can be very enjoyable.  It is easy, however, to lose yourself in the thicket while the world passes you by.  \n\nThis game is easy to pick up and easy to play.  There are no supply rules to worry about.  There are no cohesion points to finagle.  In short, this is wargaming at its most primitive.  And...for some odd reason, it works!  Perhaps it's the ferocius AI or maybe it's the simplicity.  Regardless, as the German player you feel the desperation as the Soviet hordes slowly grind you into dust.  They maneuver smartly, they attack smartly...as I said, ferocious AI.\n\nNow, this game does have its problems.  The manual is basically non-existent.  You have to figure a lot of things out on your own.  Stick with it though, and you'll soon be telling your wife \"just one more turn\" as you watch your units slowly get strangled by the Russian juggernaut.  Highly recommended--fun game that captures the spirit of the desperate Korsun defense quite well.",
                        "timestamp_created": 1540765263,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1540765263,
                        "voted_up": true,
                        "votes_up": 81,
                        "votes_funny": 0,
